  "criteria": [
    {
      "text": "lc-list: FOR and IF/ELSEIF/ELSE (nested to any allowed depth) inside LIST yield LIST_ITEMs, numbered without gaps across mixed static and generated items; items skipped by their own condition or fallback keep today's numbering rule.",
      "verify": "test",
      "evidence": null,
      "status": "pending",
      "level": "unit",
      "traces": [
        "tests/language/list-table-children.test.ts#lc-list"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lc-table: IF/ELSEIF/ELSE inside TABLE, and a FOR or IF inside either, yield ROWs; rows are padded to the widest row as before; the header rule is unchanged.",
      "verify": "test",
      "evidence": null,
      "status": "pending",
      "level": "unit",
      "traces": [
        "tests/language/list-table-children.test.ts#lc-table"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lc-close: a LIST_ITEM without END_LIST_ITEM ends at the next item, END_LIST, and now also at END_FOR, ELSE, ELSEIF or END_IF of the enclosing child block; a ROW without END_ROW does the same inside an IF or FOR that builds rows; an unclosed item followed by a FOR or IF is that item's content (no new guess), and a LIST_ITEM found inside such content is a `syntax-error` whose suggestion says to close the item with END_LIST_ITEM.",
      "verify": "test",
      "evidence": null,
      "status": "pending",
      "level": "unit",
      "traces": [
        "tests/language/list-table-children.test.ts#lc-close"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lc-errors: any other tag or non-whitespace text inside a FOR or IF that builds LIST items, or an IF that builds TABLE rows, is a `syntax-error` at its own position, in every mode; comments and whitespace are always allowed. A FOR placed directly in a TABLE keeps today's text-row fallback (a body that is not a ROW is rendered and split on `|` into a row), so no existing table template changes (question 4).",
      "verify": "test",
      "evidence": null,
      "status": "pending",
      "level": "unit",
      "traces": [
        "tests/language/list-table-children.test.ts#lc-errors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lc-limits: FOR and IF in LIST and TABLE count toward maxNodes, maxDepth (parse) and maxIterations (run) exactly as elsewhere.",
      "verify": "test",
      "evidence": null,
      "status": "pending",
      "level": "unit",
      "traces": [
        "tests/language/list-table-children.test.ts#lc-limits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lc-ws: the standalone rule and trim markers apply to the FOR, IF, ELSE and END tags in LIST and TABLE as elsewhere; LIST, TABLE and their parts keep their own spacing.",
      "verify": "test",
      "evidence": null,
      "status": "pending",
      "level": "unit",
      "traces": [
        "tests/language/list-table-children.test.ts#lc-ws"
